Sphere's apps adapt the designs of these open-source projects (no code from them is included unless stated):
  yazi (MIT), gitui (MIT), oxker (MIT), listeners (MIT), delta (MIT), herdr (Apache-2.0).

It is built on and includes these libraries, under their own licenses (MIT and/or Apache-2.0):
  Bevy, alacritty_terminal (Alacritty), portable-pty (WezTerm), rodio, hound, and the other crates listed in
  Cargo.lock.
  crates/sphere-app/src/uilayout.rs also copies part of bevy_ui 0.20.0's ui_layout_system (src/layout/mod.rs, MIT OR Apache-2.0).

The shell integration that Sphere's terminal tabs load (crates/sphere-app/assets/shell) is adapted from the shell
integration scripts of VS Code (MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation); each script says so in its header.

Sphere's voice (crates/sphere-voice):
  Kokoro-82M by hexgrad (Apache-2.0); crates/sphere-voice/assets/bm_george.f32 is its bm_george voice tensor.
  The int8 ONNX export of Kokoro from kokoro-onnx by thewh1teagle (MIT), downloaded at first use.
  misaki by hexgrad (Apache-2.0): its British lexicons (gb_gold.json, gb_silver.json) are downloaded at first use,
  and crates/sphere-voice/src/g2p.rs ports parts of its English G2P rules.
  ONNX Runtime by Microsoft (MIT), linked through the ort crate (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
  espeak-ng (GPL-3.0) is never linked or included; when installed, it is run as a separate program.

Fonts in assets/fonts are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (licence texts alongside them):
  Michroma, Rajdhani, JetBrains Mono.
